      {
        "id": 2104038588,
        "content": "This issue is the story of the snake biting its own tail. To know what scopes to request to a user, we need to know which user it is, so we need the user to log-in. But, we have to request the scopes during the login step. GitHub OAuth doesn't seem to support dynamic scopes, meaning that to change scopes the user needs to logout and login again. Afaik there is no way to also offer optional scopes, where the user could chose.\r\nI think the problem should be solved with UI changes, something like adding a button to request scopes again if the user is a member of the organization. Then, potentially that user could have access to private repos within the org.",
        "url": "https://github.com/ubiquity/work.ubq.fi/issues/41#issuecomment-2104038588",
        "commentType": "ISSUE_AUTHOR",
        "score": {
          "reward": 9.24,
          "formatting": {
            "content": {
              "p": {
                "score": 0,
                "elementCount": 2
              }
            },
            "result": 0
          },
          "priority": 3,
          "words": {
            "wordCount": 126,
            "wordValue": 0.1,
            "result": 2.44
          },
          "readability": {
            "fleschKincaid": 72.40785714285715,
            "syllables": 173,
            "sentences": 7,
            "score": 0.8759214285714285
          },
          "multiplier": 1,
          "relevance": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 2232876602,
        "content": "When a new user registers to the website and logs in via GitHub, sensitive rights are requested by the app, which is `read / write` on all `public / private` repositories. This seems to be excessive and worrisome for newcomers as they would wonder why we need to write on their private repos. Ideally, we should just request for read permission on public repos. I do not know myself the reason of the request of such elevated rights, so it would be worth investigating. If elevated rights are indeed needed for core members or insiders of the organization, these rights should be requested specifically for these members not for every new user registering.\r\n<img width=\"259\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/ubiquity/work.ubq.fi/assets/9807008/046bfa62-0eb1-4ccd-9465-315ba7c51a05\">",
        "url": "https://github.com/ubiquity/work.ubq.fi/issues/41",
        "commentType": "ISSUE_SPECIFICATION",
